  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nCooler with chances for precipitation for Friday into next week.\nWith the cooling, high temperatures on Monday will be as much as 5\nto 10 degrees below average for the mountains, valleys, and high\ndesert with high temperatures on Monday for the coast and valleys\nmostly in the 60s and lower 70s, for the lower deserts in the mid\nto upper 70s, and for the mountains in the 40s and 50s.\n\nA low pressure system moving inland through northern and central\nBaja around Friday will bring a chance of showers for late\nThursday night and Friday. A low pressure system moving inland\nthrough northern and central California on late Friday and \nSaturday will continue the chance of showers for southwestern \nCalifornia for Friday night and Saturday. Another low pressure \nsystem moving to near the California coast on late Sunday could \nbring additional rainfall to southwestern California for Sunday \nnight and Monday.",
